7 true] [17592186431535 1071 "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}+2y=0,\\,y(0)=-2,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-4.\n$$" 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431535 1072 #uuid "4d183a38-3bd7-5a3d-b0c0-6bbf656b9b64" 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431535 1074 "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-2\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+2{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +2=0.\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation can be solved by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +2 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +1)-1+2 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -1)^{2}+1 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -1)^{2} & =-1 \\\\ \\lambda -1 & =\\pm \\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =1\\pm \\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x).\n$$\n\nNow let's find the constants $P$ and $Q.$ \n\nSubstituting $y(0)=-2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nP=-2.\n$$\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\ny={e}^{x}(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x).\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=4.$ We differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}$:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={e}^{x}(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+{e}^{x}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=-4$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n-2+Q=-4\\,⟹\\,Q=-2.\n$$\n\nSo we have $P=-2$ and $Q=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-2{e}^{x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x).\n$$" 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431536 1068 #edb/ref 17592186431526 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431536 1069 "q-94027" 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431536 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431536 1071 "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+13y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x),\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+13y=0,\\,y(0)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-1.\n$$" 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431536 1072 #uuid "ad9f0a12-4237-5c82-9aa7-6fbbeb604773" 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431536 1074 "We find the constants $P$ and $Q$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nP=1.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=-1,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-2{e}^{-2x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)+{e}^{-2x}(-3P\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+3Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x).\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(0)=-1$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n-2P+3Q=-1.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $P=1$ gives $Q=\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={e}^{-2x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x+\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431537 1068 #edb/ref 17592186431521 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431537 1069 "q-130354" 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431537 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431537 1071 "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+121y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11x)+B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11x),\n$$\n\nsolve the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+121y=0,\\,y(0)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=0.\n$$" 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431537 1072 #uuid "b8669bf2-0ec8-592b-af07-c83c24aa14e8" 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431537 1074 "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=0,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=11A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11x)-11B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=0$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0=11A\\,⟹\\,A=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11x).\n$$" 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431538 1068 #edb/ref 17592186431524 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431538 1069 "q-130339" 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431538 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431538 1071 "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-9y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{3x},\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-9y=0,\\,y(0)=2,\\text{ }\\text{ }{y}^{′}(0)=0.\n$$" 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431538 1072 #uuid "cbabadfa-0d4d-5a45-80b7-bf364847e945" 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431538 1074 "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA+B=2.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=0,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-3A{e}^{-3x}+3B{e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(0)=0$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n-3A+3B=0.\n$$\n\nPutting the two equations from above together, we have the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}A+B=2 \\\\ -3A+3B=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=1,B=1.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-3x}+{e}^{3x}.\n$$" 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431539 1068 #edb/ref 17592186431525 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431539 1069 "q-130340" 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431539 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431539 1071 "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-7{y}^{′}-8y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-x}+B{e}^{8x},\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-7{y}^{′}-8y=0,\\,y(0)=0,\\text{ }\\text{ }{y}^{′}(0)=-18.\n$$" 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431539 1072 #uuid "d99b4ca2-1051-5b19-b0ca-e022766a3c13" 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431539 1074 "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA+B=0.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=-18,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-A{e}^{-x}+8B{e}^{8x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(0)=-18$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n-A+8B=-18.\n$$\n\nPutting the two equations from above together, we have the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}A+B=0 \\\\ 8B-A=-18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=2,B=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=2{e}^{-x}-2{e}^{8x}.\n$$" 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431540 1068 #edb/ref 17592186431522 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431540 1069 "q-81397" 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431540 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431540 1071 "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+3y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}x)+B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{3}x),\n$$\n\nsolve the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+3y=0,\\,y(0)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=2\\sqrt{3}.\n$$" 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431540 1072 #uuid "e50b91c5-e53d-5ab3-9544-957263ee499e" 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431540 1074 "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=2\\sqrt{3},$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=A\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{3}x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=2\\sqrt{3}$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{3}=A\\sqrt{3}\\,⟹\\,A=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}x).\n$$" 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431541 1068 #edb/ref 17592186431520 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431541 1069 "q-7789" 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431541 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431541 1071 "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}-5y=0,\\,y(1)=1,\\text{ }\\text{ }{y}^{′}(1)=7.\n$$" 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431541 1072 #uuid "fe7e11df-3bda-53fa-998a-37d8783a4f32" 13194139534661 17592186045417 true] [17592186431541 1074 "First, we find the roots of the characteristic polynomial:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda -5 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +5)(\\lambda -1) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =-5,1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-5x}+B{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nNow we find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(1)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA{e}^{-5}+Be=1.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=7,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-5A{e}^{-5x}+B{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(1)=7$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n-5A{e}^{-5}+Be=7.\n$$\n\nPutting the two equations from above together, we have the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}A{e}^{-5}+Be=1 \\\\ -5A{e}^{-5}+Be=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=-{e}^{5},B=2{e}^{-1}.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-{e}^{5}\\cdot {e}^{-5x}+2{e}^{-1}\\cdot {e}^{x} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-5x+5}+2{e}^{x-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534661 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-0137ee6e-c523-5606-ab61-bd96f6cd46e6" 17592186431455 "answer-067e7b03-611d-5b4d-b180-2ffdccf4d076" 17592186431456 "answer-0843ecfa-4e3a-592f-95c8-ebdbd00c572f" 17592186431457 "answer-090f99d5-9625-5409-8bfa-8e2c4cd59aac" 17592186431458 "answer-0922b0c1-b8d5-5acc-824f-3d66df13cd2c" 17592186431459 "answer-0d40d78b-f10f-551a-bf45-f2b3a9619d8b" 17592186431460 "answer-0db04b57-7e0b-51b5-9068-627b530d93d5" 17592186431461 "answer-1029e982-1cb8-59a1-800a-6eddc8bb0c8a" 17592186431462 "answer-1b4c76a5-9a78-55cd-9899-c617f65dbb8f" 17592186431463 "answer-1f869bf6-107f-5db7-b5a5-33d521155f66" 17592186431464 "answer-203c8f4e-c8c1-5cb3-9c03-69fcae139338" 17592186431465 "answer-204931ce-cb59-5974-b135-26060d7cd2da" 17592186431466 "answer-26037b2c-fdab-548c-ba39-81bdf3515e82" 17592186431467 "answer-2b282211-1d23-5349-b3f7-ddda48199c41" 17592186431468 "answer-3dbb7a89-524b-5fb7-8987-365ee58f1aac" 17592186431469 "answer-419328d7-32fd-5588-ac38-f02df1730edf" 17592186431470 "answer-419e161a-490d-5c6f-a7e4-eaa1b01c0887" 17592186431471 "answer-42d8c8b0-9be5-591b-b0ec-8b768f062a61" 17592186431472 "answer-454410df-f8e1-54f6-9e27-a2798142e99e" 17592186431473 "answer-462f6db9-3bd4-53ff-a35f-8656edd69646" 17592186431474 "answer-4e18fb50-aa99-53db-bb7e-d22c8a9849c1" 17592186431475 "answer-4e27ee5a-1f56-520e-bd93-b277256b9d3a" 17592186431476 "answer-50868c33-8407-589c-bfad-291f32fb6f3e" 17592186431477 "answer-596a6ddd-3d0f-5678-9be7-860b0f40740a" 17592186431478 "answer-59dfe9fd-988f-53c2-855f-b1614812537d" 17592186431479 "answer-5b280312-42b5-5848-bb8a-62dfe17d7a2d" 17592186431480 "answer-676537c8-4285-5aad-a757-a9d82bb77416" 17592186431481 "answer-697fcea0-b422-5fd9-8a3c-b4de3653327a" 17592186431482 "answer-6bd8cda8-05fa-59b2-9091-e867beec2408" 17592186431483 "answer-6e031bec-4024-5bff-a0a7-6c68243bedda" 17592186431484 "answer-7428c405-4302-51f7-bc5d-fea12e12217f" 17592186431485 "answ